quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  62,9,"O believers! When the call to prayer is made on the Day of Congregation (i.e. Friday), proceed hastily to the remembrance of Allah and leave (all) business. That would be better for you if only you knew."
  62,10,"After the prayer has ended, disperse in the land and seek Allah’s grace. And remember Allah frequently so you may be successful."
  62,11,"When they observed a (caravan with) trade or entertainment, they rushed towards it (out of dire need) and left you standing (there, during the sermon). Say: ‘Whatever is with Allah is far better than amusement and trade. And Allah is the Best of providers.’*"
  63,1,"When the hypocrites come to you (O Prophet!), they say: ‘We bear witness that you certainly are the Messenger of Allah.’ And Allah knows that you are indeed His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), but Allah bears witness that the hypocrites are surely liars."
  63,2,"They take their (false) oaths as a shield, and then they hinder (others) from the way of Allah. Evil indeed is what they used to do."
  63,3,"That is because they believed and then abandoned (their) faith. So their hearts were sealed. Hence, they do not understand."
  63,4,"When you see them, their appearance impresses you, and if they speak, you listen to their speech, but they are (just) like dried timbers leaning (against a wall). They think every cry (they hear) is against them. They are the enemy, so beware of them. May Allah destroy them. How perverted they are!"
